      "id": 1,
      "text": "Vergennes is Vermont’s first official city, chartered in 1788 and remains the only city in Addison County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sevendaysvt.com/guides/visit-vergennes-vermont-what-to-see-do-and-eat-41170739/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name honors French diplomat Charles Gravier, comte de Vergennes, who helped the American Revolution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vergennes%2C_Vermont",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Otter Creek Falls powered early mills and factories, making Vergennes a 19th‑century industrial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vergennes%2C_Vermont",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Bixby Memorial Free Library, a Greek‑Revival landmark funded by William Gove Bixby’s estate, opened in 1912.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
